1 HELP

   govax is a VAX emulator that runs VAX/VMS programs, with VMS's DCL as
   its command language.  HELP describes its commands and topics.  At
   the Topic? prompt, type:

     a topic's name            to read about it (HELP COPY, HELP SHOW
                               LOGICAL; a word may be shortened)
     INSTRUCTIONS              for more on using HELP
     HINTS                     for the topics by subject
     Return or Ctrl/Z          to leave HELP

   The machine's own commands (EXAMINE, DEPOSIT, STEP, breakpoints) are
   the debugger's: type DEBUG, then HELP at its DBG> prompt.

   Format

     HELP [keyword ...]

2 Parameter

 keyword ...

   The topic, and the subtopics below it, each a word: HELP SHOW
   LOGICAL, HELP COPY /LOG.  A word may be abbreviated as long as it is
   (HELP DIR is HELP DIRECTORY; one that fits several topics shows them
   all), and may have the wildcards * (any characters) and % (one
   character).  A word ending in "..." shows the topic and everything
   below it.  "@name" first moves to a user library (see Description).
   Without a keyword, HELP lists the main library's topics.

2 Description

   After showing a topic, HELP prompts for one of its subtopics
   ("SHOW Subtopic?"), or at the top for a topic ("Topic?").  At a
   prompt, a word shows that subtopic, "?" shows the topic again with
   its list, Return goes up a level, and Ctrl/Z ends HELP.  /NOPROMPT
   shows the topic asked for and ends.

   The main library is SYS$HELP:HELPLIB.HLB, on the system volume, or
   govax's own copy built into it when there is no such file.  The user
   libraries are those the logical names HLP$LIBRARY, HLP$LIBRARY_1,
   HLP$LIBRARY_2, ... name, in the process, group, and system tables in
   that order, each table's numbers ending at the first missing one.  A
   topic the main library doesn't have is looked for in each user
   library, and "@name" at the start of a request, or at Topic?, moves
   HELP to the user library whose name starts with name.  A help
   library is made with LIBRARY/CREATE/HELP from help files; see
   LIBRARY.

   In a command procedure, HELP's prompts read the procedure's data
   lines.  /PAGE=SAVE, /SEARCH, /EXACT, /HIGHLIGHT, /WRAP, and
   HELP/MESSAGE wait for a later version of govax, and are refused with
   %DCL-W-HELPNOTIMPL.

2 Qualifiers
/EXACT

   Not yet in govax.

/HIGHLIGHT

   Not yet in govax.

/INSTRUCTIONS

      /[NO]INSTRUCTIONS

   Shows the instructions on using HELP above the main library's list
   of topics (the default).  /NOINSTRUCTIONS shows the list alone.

/LIBLIST

      /[NO]LIBLIST

   Lists the user libraries' names after a library's list of topics
   (the default).

/LIBRARY

      /[NO]LIBRARY[=filespec]

   /LIBRARY=filespec makes the library named the main one, its name
   parsed with the default SYS$HELP:.HLB.  /NOLIBRARY makes the first
   user library the main one.

/MESSAGE

   Not yet in govax.

/OUTPUT

      /[NO]OUTPUT[=filespec]

   Writes the help to a file, HELP.LIS by default, rather than the
   terminal, with lists 132 columns wide.  /NOOUTPUT writes nothing.

/PAGE

      /[NO]PAGE[=keyword]

   Stops after each screenful, as TYPE/PAGE does.  CLEAR_SCREEN (the
   default) clears the screen before each topic, and SCROLL doesn't.
   Without /PAGE or /NOPAGE, HELP pages when it writes to a terminal.

/PROMPT

      /[NO]PROMPT

   Prompts for further topics after the first (the default).

/SEARCH

   Not yet in govax.

/USERLIBRARY

      /[NO]USERLIBRARY[=(table[,...])]

   The tables whose HLP$LIBRARY names are searched: PROCESS, GROUP,
   SYSTEM, ALL (the default), or NONE.  /NOUSERLIBRARY is NONE.

/WRAP

   Not yet in govax.

2 Examples

   1.$ HELP

     Lists the topics, then prompts for one.

   2.$ HELP SHOW LOGICAL

     Shows SHOW LOGICAL, then prompts for its subtopics.

   3.$ HELP/NOPROMPT COPY /RECORD_FORMAT

     Shows COPY's /RECORD_FORMAT qualifier, and ends.

   4.$ DEFINE HLP$LIBRARY DUA1:[TOOLS]TOOLS.HLB
     $ HELP @TOOLS

     Makes TOOLS.HLB a user library, and shows its topics.
